  "notes": "PROMPT_GT_MISMATCH: prompt says Security Hub is enabled in the audit account \"as the delegated administrator\" but the ground truth never designates a delegated admin (no Organizations admin-account call); omitted. The landing-zone rule accepts any pattern mentioning landing zone, because the ground truth uses a custom superwerker event and real Control Tower uses SetupLandingZone/UpdateLandingZone; for the same reason it can't be pinned to the Control Tower source. Workflow checks look for API names (InviteMembers, CreateMembers, AcceptInvitation, EnableSecurityHub, in API, boto3 or CLI spelling), not description text or step names. iam_roles needs only one role: a single role trusted by both events and ssm is a valid design, and events_invoke_role / automation_assume_role cover the two uses. read_parameters_permission accepts a Resource of * as well as the /superwerker/ path. Real-output review (2026-11-10): DSV4F has no rules or documents and OpenCode_DSV4F only a Command stub, so their failures are genuine. Gemini38F's account rule fires on any CreateManagedAccount without the SUCCEEDED state, and it uses auto-enable without invite or accept steps; kept."
}
